      <marc:subfield code="a">Yasutaka Kanda, 53 years old, is one of only two barbers in town. Lately, he&apos;s been troubled by his son, who’s known for never sticking to anything for long. Now the son claims he wants to “revive the hometown” and has decided to return to this rural village—where cows outnumber people—to take over the barbershop. Kanda feels both anxious and concerned. It’s not that he doesn’t love this land, but he believes young people should step onto a broader stage. Staying in a town with no future might only lead to all their energy and potential being swallowed up</marc:subfield>
